  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Absolute and relative superlative",
     "texto": [
      "To say that something is «very» or «extremely» + adjective, add the suffix **-issimo/a/i/e** (*bellissimo*, *grandissima*, *carissimi*), equivalent to **molto + adjective**.",
      "The relative superlative («the most of all») uses **definite article + più/meno + adjective**: **il più caro**, **la meno cara**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Key irregular forms",
     "texto": [
      "As adjectives: **buono → migliore** (better), **cattivo → peggiore** (worse). As adverbs with verbs: **bene → meglio** (better), **male → peggio** (worse).",
      "**Questo ristorante è il migliore** (adjective); **Qui si mangia meglio** (adverb with a verb)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Irregular forms",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Positive",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Comparative adjective",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Comparative adverb",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
